- Change summary:
  - Replaced `SYSCTL__vRegisterIRQVectorHandler(...)` with `SYSCTL__enRegisterIRQVectorHandler(...)` returning `SYSCTL_nERROR` and propagating the fixed-vector SCB registration status.
  - Restored the user-requested old cast-style null check in the SYSCTL IRQ-register wrapper and kept the existing null-handler no-op behavior, now returning `SYSCTL_enERROR_OK` on that path.
  - Replaced `SYSCTL__vEnInterruptVector(...)` and `SYSCTL__vDisInterruptVector(...)` with `SYSCTL__enEnableInterruptVector(...)` and `SYSCTL__enDisableInterruptVector(...)`, both returning the underlying NVIC status as `SYSCTL_nERROR`.
  - Updated `SYSCTL__enInit(...)` so IRQ-registration, vector-enable, and vector-disable failures stop the ordered init sequence and propagate to the caller.
  - Updated focused host tests so the new SCB/NVIC failure-propagation paths are asserted explicitly instead of only checking delegation side effects.
- Post-implementation audit:
  - The SYSCTL application-layer wrappers in the current tree now align with the existing SYSEXC/SYSTICK enum-returning wrapper pattern.
  - No additional SYSCTL application-layer `void` wrappers that discard enum-returning SCB/NVIC status were found in this follow-up pass.
  - Older void-wrapper outliers still exist in other modules such as TIMER, but those are outside the current SYSCTL request and were left untouched.